{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Types of Cloud Computing Services"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about cloud computing services."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.   Interpret the IT needs assessment, to determine the required technology to manage information, according to the rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present Passive in Affirmative Statements and Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When we want to emphasize the object of a sentence or when the subject is not important or unknown, we use the <span class =\"strong\">passive voice</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": " The <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">passive voice</span></span> is used in the <span class=\"italic\">simple present</span> to talk about situations that occur on a regular basis. Generally, the doer of the action is unknown or is not relevant.</br></br>  To make the simple present passive in <span class=\"italic\">affirmative form</span>, the verb <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">to be</span></span>  is used in the <span class=\"italic\">present simple</span> as an auxiliary, followed by the main verb in the past <span class=\"italic\">participle form</span>:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Object</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Verb to be</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Main verb</br> (past participle)</span></div>\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Complement</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Cloud services</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">are</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">outsourced</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">to reduce costs.</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To make the simple present passive in the <span class=\"strong\">question form</span>, the verb <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">to be</span></span> is used in the present simple as an auxiliary at the beginning of the question followed by the object, and then the main verb in the past participle form:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Verb to be</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Object</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Main verb</br>(past participle)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Complement + ?</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Are</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">these services</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">delivered</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">considering the client's needs?</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How are cloud services classified?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sarah, how are these services delivered?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "These services are often outsourced."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Managed clouds, which are like private clouds but are owned and managed by the customer himself."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Understanding the concepts of public clouds, private clouds, hybrid clouds and managed clouds"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Cloud computing services can be classified into four types:"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Public Clouds</span></br> This type of service is offered to multiple users at the same time. The service is not designed with a particular client in mind.</br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Private Clouds</span></br> It is a product specially designed for organizations, which are looking for the benefits of cloud services, but need to offer customized services and have control over them.</br></br>   <span class=\"strong\">Hybrid Clouds</span></br> Some organizations have both public and private cloud services, depending on the type of information they handle. The public might have free access to certain content, but some sensitive data would be stored under strict security protocols and have restricted access.</br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Managed Clouds</span></br> This type of cloud service is similar to private clouds. The main difference is that the customer owns and manages the computing services."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "physical   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "existing in a physical way that can be seen and touched"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's basically a provision of technological services in which some functions aren't in a physical room, but over the internet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "potential  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an expected ability or characteristic"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Cloud services have transformed the way the technology industry works because of its potential to save costs, flexibility and accessibility."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flexibility "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the quality of being able to be customized or adapted, depending on the needs or situation "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Cloud services have transformed the way the technology industry works because of its potential to save costs, flexibility and accessibility."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rental  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "paying an amount of money for using a service temporarily "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Infrastructure as a Service (IAAS), which is the rental of IT equipment from a cloud services provider."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hybrid  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a mixture between two or more things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A hybrid cloud shares characteristics of both public and privates clouds."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "security protocol"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a system of rules that states what to do under certain circumstances related to data security "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When a company offers content with free access to interact with the public, but at the same time there are security protocols for restricted data and computing services."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find information about 3 companies that use cloud computing services."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Analyze what the companies do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Propose what kind of cloud the companies use."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a chart comparing the information you found."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your work with your classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about 3 companies that use cloud computing services."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I analyze what the companies do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I propose the cloud that each company uses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a chart comparing the 3 companies and their clouds."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my work with classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n7le01ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Professor</span>: Good morning, class. Today, we'll be talking about cloud computing services. But first, what is understood by a cloud computing service, Sarah?</div><div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Sarah</span>: Well, it's basically a provision of technological services in which some functions aren't in a physical room, but over the internet. These services are often outsourced.</div><div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Professor</span>: That's right. Cloud services have transformed the way the technology industry works because of its potential to save costs, flexibility and accessibility. Charles, how are cloud services classified?</div>"}, {"time": "33500", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Charles</span>: These services are classified into three main categories in terms of property. First, there is Software as a Service (SAAS), in which software is made available over a network and it's no longer acquired through licenses. Then we have Infrastructure as a Service (IAAS), which is the rental of IT equipment from a cloud services provider, which replaces the need of owning computers, networks and expensive storage devices. Finally we find Platform as a Service (PAAS), which basically allows users to develop and execute their own applications over an external platform.</div><div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Professor</span>: Well summarized, Charles. Sarah, how are these services delivered?</div>"}, {"time": "79000", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Sarah</span>: Hmm, cloud computing services delivery is divided into four types: public, private, hybrid and managed clouds. A public cloud allows users free access and provides the greatest level of efficiency such as in emails or social networking sites. A private cloud, which is maintained on a private network, for example in a company, is much safer than a public one, and allows companies to reduce costs, saving on infrastructure. A hybrid cloud shares characteristics of both public and private clouds, for example when a company offers content with free access to interact with the public, but at the same time, there are security protocols for restricted data and computing services. Finally, managed clouds, which are like private clouds, but are owned and managed by the customer himself.</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n7le01ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": "Ahogado img1.jpg", "type": "img"}], "type": "static", "template_override": 1, "id": 2, "title": ""}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": "01 (1).jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "02 (1).jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "03 (1).jpg", "type": "img"}], "type": "static", "template_override": 1, "id": 3, "title": ""}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list different kinds of cloud computing services. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about different characteristics for cloud computing services. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss the differences among public clouds, private clouds, hybri